$ =====================================================================
$ RBE3 TEST SERIES -- Deck 14: reference grid with a rotated OUTPUT
$ coordinate system (CD field) -- general coverage, exercises a code
$ path (basic-to-local coordinate transform of the RBE3 result) that
$ no other deck in this series touches.
$
$ CORD2R 20 is a system rotated 30 degrees about the basic Z-axis.
$ Grid 900 (the RBE3 reference/dependent grid) has CD=20, so its
$ reported displacement/rotation should come out expressed in this
$ rotated frame, not in basic coordinates.
$
$ Independent grids 901-904 remain in basic coordinates (CD=0,
$ default) and are driven by SPC to an exact rigid-body field in
$ BASIC coordinates:
$     U0    = ( 0.20, -0.15,  0.30)   (basic)
$     omega = ( 0.10,  0.05, -0.12)   (basic)
$
$ Expected result, grid 900, reported in the CD=20 (rotated) frame:
$   T1=0.098205  T2=-0.229904  T3=0.300000
$   R1=0.111603  R2=-0.006699  R3=-0.120000
$ (= U0/omega rotated 30 degrees about Z into the local frame --
$ T3/R3 unaffected since Z is the rotation axis and both fields have
$ no other Z-axis-orthogonal peculiarity)
$ =====================================================================
SOL 101
CEND
DISP = ALL
SPC = 1
BEGIN BULK
$
CORD2R,20,0,0.,0.,0.,0.,0.,1.,+CR20
+CR20,0.8660254,0.5,0.
$
GRID,900,,0.,0.,0.,20
$
GRID,901,,1.5,0.8,-0.4
GRID,902,,-1.0,1.2,0.6
GRID,903,,0.5,-1.5,0.9
GRID,904,,-0.8,-0.6,-1.1
$
GRID,800,,10.,10.,10.
GRID,801,,11.,10.,10.
MAT1,1,1.,,0.
PROD,1,1,1.
CROD,91,1,800,801
$
RBE3    60              900     123456  1.0     123     901     1.0     +A1
+A1     123     902     1.0     123     903     1.0     123     904
$
SPC,1,901,1,0.276
SPC,1,901,2,-0.29
SPC,1,901,3,0.305
SPC,1,901,456,0.
$
SPC,1,902,1,0.374
SPC,1,902,2,-0.09
SPC,1,902,3,0.47
SPC,1,902,456,0.
$
SPC,1,903,1,0.065
SPC,1,903,2,-0.3
SPC,1,903,3,0.125
SPC,1,903,456,0.
$
SPC,1,904,1,0.073
SPC,1,904,2,0.056
SPC,1,904,3,0.28
SPC,1,904,456,0.
$
SPC,1,800,123456,0.
$
ENDDATA
